course: dictionary
lesson: 11295
title: Words about the sea
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A yacht is a boat with sails, and people use it for racing or for fun. When you meet this word, look for clues around it, such as sails, wind, water or a race. Those clues tell you the word is about boats.
explain: «The yachts raced across the bay as the wind filled their sails.» The wind fills the sails, so the yachts move, and racing shows they are sailing boats. Try swapping in "boats with sails" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some yachts are not small sailing boats at all. «The luxury yacht had its own swimming pool.» Luxury and a swimming pool tell you this yacht is huge and expensive, the kind a very rich person might own for holidays or parties.
explain: The word is said like "yot", even though the spelling has a "ch" that you do not say. Context helps again: if a sentence mentions a holiday, a race or the sea, you can guess that yacht means a boat.
fact: A yacht is a boat with sails, used for racing or for pleasure.
fact: A yacht can also be a large, expensive motor boat or ship, often owned by a very rich person.
fact: To go yachting means to sail for fun.
fact: A yacht race is often held as part of a regatta, which is a set of boat races.
fact: A sailing yacht moves because the wind pushes on its sails.
exercise: «The yachts raced across the bay as the wind filled their sails.» What is a yacht in this sentence? | A bird that flies over the sea | *A boat with sails | A large fish | A kind of sweet
exercise: «The luxury yacht had its own swimming pool.» What does the word luxury tell you? | The yacht sinks quickly | The yacht is small and old | The yacht is made of wood | *The yacht is large and expensive
exercise: Sam says yacht means a kind of cake. What do the clues in «Mum and Dad went yachting on the lake at the weekend» show? | Baking a cake for a party | A visit to a sweet shop | *Sailing a boat for fun | A school trip to the shops
test: The yac
